    "Transfer from perindopril relies on structural analogy to an ACE-inhibitor prodrug rather than an identical compound.",
    "No measured permeability, solubility, or first-pass data for the query molecule."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because the most transferable evidence, perindopril (structurally related ACE-inhibitor ester prodrug), shows absolute oral bioavailability of 66-95% in fasted subjects and 30 ± 6% in cirrhotic patients, both above threshold; L3 exposure records for unrelated molecules add no contradictory evidence, and no affirmative low-F evidence applies to fosinopril."
}

